domain TEST_AUTHORITY_V2:
  description "Decision gate for repository-wide Seal-based test authority."

problem P1:
  |
    Decide the next authorized change after the owner established that an unsealed
    test has no adequate stated basis, and that a sealed test is evidence only for
    the exact Cause revision on which its verification Seal depends.

evidence E1:
  |
    On 2026-09-16 the product owner confirmed that tests without a Seal are invalid
    as evidence, and that a sealed test becomes invalid for a later/current claim
    when its basis is stale or progresses, while remaining valid for its original
    historical basis.

evidence E2:
  |
    scripts/test-authority.mjs currently classifies discovered tests absent from
    scripts/test-authority-inventory.json as active with reason ungoverned and runs
    them, while warning that their results are not SealGraph validity evidence.

evidence E3:
  |
    The same selector already disables configured verification REFs for missing or
    wrong source binding, source divergence, and direct or transitive SealGraph
    staleness. SealGraph defines staleness from immutable Seals plus current REF
    heads, so historical Seals are not erased by later REF progress.

evidence E4:
  |
    Repository guidance requires a review-gate or user-confirmed operational
    decision to be recorded in an ADR, and requires ADR-0015 and later to remain
    Proposed until the decision owner approves the exact ADR revision.

premise SCOPE:
  |
    Preserve all test files and historical Seals. Change only current evidence
    eligibility and its reporting. Do not commit, push, deploy, or activate external
    systems in this slice.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Implement immediately without an ADR; infer acceptance of an unseen ADR revision;
    or draft the exact Proposed ADR and its Japanese review projection, then wait for
    exact-revision acceptance before changing the selector and sealing verification.

pending U1:
  |
    The owner has confirmed the policy semantics but has not yet reviewed a named
    ADR-0034 revision and its complete wording.

decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4, SCOPE, OPTIONS, U1:
  |
    Draft ADR-0034 revision one as Proposed and present its complete Japanese review
    scope. Do not change test selection or create implementation and verification
    Seals until the owner explicitly accepts that exact revision.

decision D2 based_on D1, E1, E2, E3, SCOPE:
  |
    After exact-revision acceptance, change unlisted tests from active/ungoverned to
    disabled/unsealed, retain the existing source and staleness gates, report exact
    current evidence eligibility without deleting historical validity, and seal the
    selector verification against the accepted authority.
